            <ArticleTitle>[The use of central electroanalgesia in the combined sanatorium-health resort treatment of patients with ischemic heart disease and hypertension].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>36-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Hemodynamics was studied in coronary patients with essential hypertension. The principal parameters of circulation showed positive dynamics induced by central electroanalgesia (LENAR apparatus) under varying pulse recurrence rate. Group I patients underwent the procedure at a frequency of 500-700 Hz, group II patients at that of 900-1000 Hz. Control patients received imitated procedures. Central electroanalgesia at a frequency of 900-1000 Hz produced the most pronounced effect on the clinical symptoms, myocardial contractility and total peripheral resistance.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
